course: dictionary
lesson: 2579
title: Who counts the people?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A demographer is a scientist who studies populations. A population is all the people who live in one place, such as a town, a country or the whole world.
explain: Demographers count and study numbers: how many people live somewhere, how old they are, and how many are born, die or move away. They look at population trends, which means how these numbers change over time. «Demographers predict» how many children will need school places in a few years.
explain: Demographers also study the past. «Population experts (demographers) estimate about 3.5 to 5 million Holodomor deaths in Soviet Ukraine.» An estimate is a careful best guess from the records. Most demographers do not support older, much higher figures, because the evidence does not back them up.
fact: A demographer is a scientist who studies populations.
fact: A population is all the people who live in one place.
fact: Demographers look at how many people there are, how old they are, and how many are born, die or move.
fact: Governments use demographers' work to plan schools, hospitals and homes.
fact: «Birth rate» means how many babies are born in a place over a set time.
exercise: What does a demographer study? | Rocks and fossils | The weather and the rain | * Populations: how many people live in a place, how old they are, and how many are born, die or move
exercise: Which list shows what a demographer finds out about a town? | * How many people live there, how old they are, and how many are born or move away | The colour of the houses | How tall the trees are
exercise: A government wants to build new schools. Which expert would help it most? | A pilot, who flies planes | A gardener, who plants flowers | A chef, who cooks meals | * A demographer, who predicts how many children will live in the town
test: A census is a count of everyone in a country. Why might a demographer use one? | To count the trees in a park | To choose the colour of a new school | To write a story about a king | * To find out how many people live there and how the population is changing
test: Which phrase means how the numbers of people change over time? | * Population trends | Loud music | Tall buildings | Fast cars
exam: What is a demographer? | A person who makes maps of mountains | A teacher who checks spelling | A doctor who treats sick people | * A scientist who studies populations, such as how many people live in a place
